const s = $('Check Settings').first().json;
const threads = $('Find Unanswered').all();
const esc = t => String(t ?? '').replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');

// The AI step returns one result per thread, in the same order.
const due = $input.all()
  .map((item, i) => ({ t: threads[i].json, ai: item.json.output || {} }))
  .filter(x => x.ai.expects_reply);
if (!due.length) return [];

const lines = [`⏰ <b>${due.length} sent email${due.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} still waiting for a reply</b>`];
for (const { t, ai } of due) {
  lines.push('', `<b>${esc(t.subject)}</b>`);
  lines.push(`To ${esc(t.to)} · ${t.daysWaiting} days · <a href="${t.link}">open thread</a>`);
  if (ai.waiting_for) lines.push(`Waiting for: ${esc(ai.waiting_for)}`);
  if (s.includeNudges && ai.nudge) lines.push(`<i>Suggested follow-up:</i>\n${esc(ai.nudge)}`);
}

// Telegram allows 4,096 characters per message, so split long messages on line breaks.
const chunks = [];
let cur = '';
for (const l of lines) {
  if (cur && (cur + '\n' + l).length > 3900) { chunks.push(cur); cur = l; }
  else cur = cur ? cur + '\n' + l : l;
}
if (cur.trim()) chunks.push(cur);
return chunks.map(text => ({ json: { text } }));
